 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse of the veterinarian directory: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic therefore publishes a second, read-only view of the same directory (confirmed 2026-08-08) `[REQ-VET-003]`. It lists every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it. All specialties appear together on one page rather than a page at a time. Each veterinarian is shown by full name, first name before last name. The page lists specialties rather than the roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears on it nowhere. The view only reads; managing veterinarians or their specialties stays out of scope under NG-2.
+
+This request deliberately gives the page no visible entry point: no navigation entry and no link from another page. Its own address, `/specialties.html`, is therefore the only way in. The page itself still carries the site-wide navigation every page carries. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request — see [Open Questions](#open-questions).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the specialty directory is opened, then each holder is listed under it by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given more specialties than the veterinarian directory would show on one page, when the specialty directory is opened, then all of them are listed together, without paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the specialty directory's address, when it is requested directly, then the page is served, and no other page links to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. When the clinic knows no specialties at all, the page still renders rather than failing.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are listed in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. A specialty's stored name is data rather than interface wording, so it is shown as stored in every supported language.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
